# What Docker never needs to receive.
#
# Without this file the whole working tree is sent to the daemon as build
# context, .git included, while the Dockerfile copies four directories. The
# context is transferred before the first instruction runs, so it is paid on
# every build, including the ones that hit the layer cache and produce nothing.
#
# Measured: 637 MB of context before, 586 MB after — 52 MB saved, almost all of
# it the .git directory.
#
# The remaining 575 MB is `un_cards/`, and that is not excluded here because
# the Dockerfile genuinely copies it: the UN card export serves those PDFs.
# It is by far the largest thing in the image and worth a decision rather than
# a default; docs/data-sources.md states what it costs and what it buys.

.git
.github
.gitignore

# Node dependencies are installed inside the frontend build stage.
node_modules
frontend/node_modules
frontend/dist

# Python bytecode and virtualenvs.
__pycache__
**/__pycache__
*.py[cod]
.venv
venv

# Local runtime data: the database, exports and the generated secret key. Never
# part of an image, and shipping them would mean shipping someone's data.
data
exports

# Test and tooling output.
.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache
.mypy_cache
coverage
htmlcov
*.log

# Documentation and repository furniture. The application does not read these —
# except the changelog, which the what's-new card serves after an update.
docs
*.md
!backend/**/*.md
!CHANGELOG.md
scripts
unraid
assets

# Editor and OS noise.
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
